course: dictionary
lesson: 7037
title: Partner: someone who does it with you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A partner is someone you do something together with. You can work, play or dance with a partner. Look at the words around the word to find its meaning: «Turn to your partner and count the apples in the basket.» The words turn to and count tell you a partner is the person sitting next to you, working with you.
explain: Partner can also be a number pair. In maths, 3 and 7 are partners for 10, because they go together to make 10. A business partner is one of the owners of a business, sharing its work and its money. Try your meaning in the sentence: does "the person sitting next to you" fit? Yes, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «In Toronto, Sofia meets her dad's partner's two girls at a barbecue.» Here partner means the person a grown-up lives with or is married to. Clues: dad, girls and a barbecue show a family. Partner can mean different things, so the clues around it matter most.
fact: A partner is a person who does something together with you.
fact: Partner can mean a work partner, a dance partner, or a partner in a game.
fact: In maths, number partners are two numbers that make a total: 3 and 7 are partners for 10.
fact: A business partner is one of the owners of a business.
fact: «Plus-one» means the guest or partner you are allowed to bring to an event.
exercise: In maths, 3 and 7 are partners for 10. What does partners mean here? | *Numbers that go together to make a total | Two dogs playing in a park | Two shop owners arguing | Two numbers that are never added
exercise: «Turn to your partner and share your ideas.» What does partner mean here? | A shopkeeper who sells sweets | *The person next to you, working together | A prize for the winner | A parent who lives in another town
exercise: Which word describes someone who owns a business with you? | Classmate on a trip | *Business partner | Dance teacher | Plus-one
test: «Plus-one» means the guest or partner you are allowed to bring to an event. What does plus-one mean? | A friend who lives next door | A number you add to ten | *The guest or partner you may bring along | A ticket that costs more money
test: Which pair of numbers are partners that make 10? | 4 and 4 and 4 | 1 and 1 | 2 and 5 | *3 and 7
exam: Using the sentence «Turn to your partner», what does partner mean? | A friend you have never met | A teacher in charge of the class | A parent who lives in another town | *The person beside you, doing the task together
